module std.judgment_contract
// THE SEMANTIC CONTRACT OF A DEMAND, BELOW ANY DECISION ABOUT STORING ONE.
//
// What a judgment IS -- its subject, the inputs its result depends on, the shape of that result,
// and the identity derived from them -- is a fact about MEANING. Whether an answer is persisted,
// where, under which provider, with what retention, is a fact about REALIZATION. Those are two
// layers and this module is the lower one.
//
// THEY WERE ONE MODULE AND THE FORK WAS STRUCTURAL, NOT STYLISTIC. `std.materialization_provider`
// carries the persistence projection, and it legitimately depends on
// `v2.compiler.self_host.generation` for the pre-materialization identity a stored artifact is
// keyed against. So a consumer that wanted only `JudgmentContract` -- the native compiler's own
// scheduler, which persists nothing -- had to drag that dependency into its production entry
// closure to get it. It did: the demand-engine cut pulled `self_host.generation` into
// `v2.compiler.compile` and the emitted crate stopped building, on a realization defect in a
// module the scheduler never calls. The import edge was the defect's carrier; this split removes
// the edge rather than patching what it exposed.
//
// NOTHING HERE KNOWS ABOUT A STORE. No provider, no request family, no address, no retention. A
// declaration that needs one of those belongs in the provider above, and the direction of that
// dependency is the whole point: meaning does not import storage.

import std.types { Bool, Int, List, String, NonEmptyStr }
import std.cache_identity { ArtifactKindId }
import std.content_hash { ContentHash, Fnv1a64Structural, fnv1a64_structural_hex_digest }
import std.dissolution { DissolutionCondition, unbound_dissolution }


// PROGRESS ON THE CARVE-OUT ABOVE, stated narrowly so it is not read as the dissolution: the
// persistent-store realization (std.materialization_object store_lookup_decide) now mints its
// ProbeFound from the stored BYTES -- payload_part derives every part digest and size from the
// payload, and store_observed_digest folds them -- so on that route observed_digest is computed,
// not asserted. The carve-out still stands for every other caller, because ProbeFound remains
// freely constructible; its trigger (constructor confinement of ProviderProbe) is unchanged.

// Computation identity is CONSUMED, never re-invented (mandate rule; DESIGN duplicate-work thread):
// the ComputationIdentity qualification belongs to the materialize spine (v2.std.materialize is the
// structural-corner qualifier; std.computation_identity is the lattice authority). This slice
// grounds exactly the StructurallyIdentical corner, because the exact structural content key is the
// only sharing that key JUSTIFIES — and it DERIVES that grade from the binding it computes rather
// than accepting one (see the derivation note below, review 44265). Advertising normalized or
// extensional sharing while executing structural equality would be a fabricated capability, so
// those grades are not reachable here at all; they arrive by the spine widening the KEY, not by
// anyone passing a grade.

// Relation to std.cache_interface (the shape/transport/policy cut, DESIGN section 3):
// CacheLookupResult / CacheRejectReason are BACKEND-grain — what one storage backend said, with
// producer receipts and transport faults (BackendUnavailable, TransportFaithfulnessFailure). This
// contract is CONSUMER-grain: given what the realization found at the key (ProviderProbe), decide
// serve or typed refusal under the request's correctness demands (declared-input key, artifact
// kind, content verification, artifact completeness, identity grade). Backend faults stay in
// CacheRejectReason at the transport and are deliberately not restated here; a transport that
// cannot probe refuses at its own layer and no ProviderProbe is fabricated.

// The artifact-completeness rule: an artifact carries ALL correctness-relevant outputs of the
// transform it memoizes, including the compile-clean diagnostic union — a cached parse that dropped
// its diagnostics would green a red, which is the fabricated-plausible-output arm section 5
// forbids. The rule has TWO halves and both are load-bearing: the obligation roster is derived from
// the request (below), and the SATISFACTION roster is derived from the payload — carried outputs
// are digested parts whose fold IS the artifact's content digest, so a claimed-but-absent output is
// caught by the read-back comparison rather than believed (codex review 44278; the payload-binding
// note carries the reasoning). Completeness is enforced on BOTH doors, and BOTH doors derive every
// obligation FROM THE REQUEST (operator rework ruling, PR 7385 blocker 1): provider_admit takes the
// ArtifactRequest itself — there is no caller-supplied required_outputs parameter, so a weakened
// obligation list is UNWRITABLE at the admission door by construction — and checks kind, request
// key, content digest, completeness, and identity grade before any byte enters the store;
// provider_serve runs the same request_artifact_binding as the validation backstop for pre-contract
// artifacts already on disk. The obligation roster itself is derived from the request COPRODUCT
// (codex review 44175), so 'admit against a weakened roster' is not merely unavailable at the door
// — it is unrepresentable in the request. FIRST NAMED CONSUMER TARGET:
// extdeps.realization.resolved_graph's disk-hit refusal
// (resolved_graph_cache_faithful_probe_support_dissolve_trigger) — the modeled disk probe is
// intentionally not entered on v1 because the cache format still exposes only the whole payload
// digest and payload byte count, not per-output digests or byte sizes for
// resolved_graph/source_indices; the transport refuses faithfully before provider_serve and
// dissolves when the artifact FORMAT_VERSION persists those faithful parts so the probe can be
// constructed through the interpreter instead of by fabrication.

// Declared-input order is part of the key: declared_inputs_digest folds in list order, so the
// REQUESTER owes a canonical input order (the same duty artifact_key_hash discharges by fixed field
// order). Two requests that differ only by input permutation key apart — a loud miss, never a wrong
// hit — so the fail-open direction is closed; the canonical-order duty is on the constructor rows
// below, which fix an order by construction.

type ArtifactOutputId = NonEmptyStr where brand("ArtifactOutputId")


data output_parse_tree: ArtifactOutputId = "parse_tree"

data output_parse_diagnostics: ArtifactOutputId = "parse_diagnostics"

data output_typed_module_interface: ArtifactOutputId = "typed_module_interface"

data output_typecheck_diagnostics: ArtifactOutputId = "typecheck_diagnostics"

data output_resolved_graph: ArtifactOutputId = "resolved_graph"

data output_source_indices: ArtifactOutputId = "source_indices"

data output_compile_clean_diagnostic_union: ArtifactOutputId = "compile_clean_diagnostic_union"

data output_native_compiler_executable: ArtifactOutputId = "native_compiler_executable"

data output_native_compiler_build_diagnostics: ArtifactOutputId = "native_compiler_build_diagnostics"

data output_universe_test_identity_population: ArtifactOutputId = "universe_test_identity_population"

data output_universe_module_import_closures: ArtifactOutputId = "universe_module_import_closures"

data output_module_test_verdicts: ArtifactOutputId = "module_test_verdicts"

data output_module_preparation_diagnostics: ArtifactOutputId = "module_preparation_diagnostics"


type DeclaredInput {
  ref: NonEmptyStr
  digest: Fnv1a64Structural
}


type OccurrencePersistenceContract
  = SemanticOnly
  | Scoped
  | Rebinding


type PersistedOutputObligation {
  id: ArtifactOutputId
  occurrence_contract: OccurrencePersistenceContract
}


type ResultContract {
  carries_semantic_value: Bool
  ordered_diagnostics: Bool
  carries_effect_requests_receipts: Bool
  carries_refusal_arm: Bool
  required_persisted_outputs: List<PersistedOutputObligation>
}


fn persisted_output(
  id: ArtifactOutputId,
  occurrence_contract: OccurrencePersistenceContract
) -> PersistedOutputObligation {
  PersistedOutputObligation { id: id, occurrence_contract: occurrence_contract }
}


type DemandIdentity {
  kind: ArtifactKindId
  subject: Fnv1a64Structural
  declared_inputs: List<DeclaredInput>
}


type LengthPrefixedField {
  value: String
  rest: String
}


type LengthPrefixedScan {
  i: Int
  hit: Int?
}


type DecodedDeclaredInputs {
  inputs: List<DeclaredInput>
  rest: String
}


fn string_from_code_points(cs: List<Int>) -> String {
  join(cs |> map(c => from_code_point(cp: c)), "")
}


fn length_prefixed_encode(s: String) -> String {
  join([to_string(s.length()), "#", s], "")
}


fn length_prefixed_decode(s: String) -> LengthPrefixedField? {
  let cs = chars(s: s)
  let scan = cs |> fold(
    init: LengthPrefixedScan { i: 0, hit: none },
    f: (st, c) =>
      match st.hit {
        Present { value: _ } => st
        Absent =>
          if c == 35 {
            LengthPrefixedScan { i: st.i, hit: Present { value: st.i } }
          } else {
            LengthPrefixedScan { i: st.i + 1, hit: none }
          }
      }
  )
  match scan.hit {
    Absent => none
    Present { value: hash_at } => {
      let len_text = string_from_code_points(cs: cs |> take(n: hash_at))
      let after = string_from_code_points(cs: cs |> skip(n: hash_at + 1))
      match parse_int(s: len_text) {
        Absent => none
        Present { value: n } =>
          if n < 0 {
            none
          } else {
            let after_cs = chars(s: after)
            if (after_cs |> count()) < n {
              none
            } else {
              Present {
                value: LengthPrefixedField {
                  value: string_from_code_points(cs: after_cs |> take(n: n)),
                  rest: string_from_code_points(cs: after_cs |> skip(n: n))
                }
              }
            }
          }
      }
    }
  }
}


fn decode_declared_inputs(remaining: Int, rest: String, acc: List<DeclaredInput>) -> DecodedDeclaredInputs? {
  if remaining == 0 {
    Present { value: DecodedDeclaredInputs { inputs: acc, rest: rest } }
  } else {
    match length_prefixed_decode(s: rest) {
      Absent => none
      Present { value: ref_f } =>
        match length_prefixed_decode(s: ref_f.rest) {
          Absent => none
          Present { value: dig_f } =>
            match fnv1a64_structural_hex_digest(hex: dig_f.value) {
              Absent => none
              Present { value: digest } =>
                decode_declared_inputs(
                  remaining: remaining - 1,
                  rest: dig_f.rest,
                  acc: concat(acc, [DeclaredInput { ref: ref_f.value as NonEmptyStr, digest: digest }])
                )
            }
        }
    }
  }
}


fn demand_identity_canonical(demand: DemandIdentity) -> NonEmptyStr {
  let inputs_enc = demand.declared_inputs |> fold(
    init: "",
    f: (acc, i) => concat(
      concat(acc, length_prefixed_encode(s: i.ref as String)),
      length_prefixed_encode(s: i.digest.digest as String)
    )
  )
  concat(
    concat(
      concat(
        length_prefixed_encode(s: "demand"),
        length_prefixed_encode(s: demand.kind as String)
      ),
      length_prefixed_encode(s: demand.subject.digest as String)
    ),
    concat(length_prefixed_encode(s: to_string(demand.declared_inputs |> count())), inputs_enc)
  ) as NonEmptyStr
}


fn demand_identity_decode(encoded: String) -> DemandIdentity? {
  match length_prefixed_decode(s: encoded) {
    Absent => none
    Present { value: tag } =>
      if (tag.value == "demand") == false {
        none
      } else {
        match length_prefixed_decode(s: tag.rest) {
          Absent => none
          Present { value: kind_f } =>
            match length_prefixed_decode(s: kind_f.rest) {
              Absent => none
              Present { value: sub_f } =>
                match length_prefixed_decode(s: sub_f.rest) {
                  Absent => none
                  Present { value: n_f } =>
                    match parse_int(s: n_f.value) {
                      Absent => none
                      Present { value: n } =>
                        match fnv1a64_structural_hex_digest(hex: sub_f.value) {
                          Absent => none
                          Present { value: subject } =>
                            match decode_declared_inputs(remaining: n, rest: n_f.rest, acc: []) {
                              Absent => none
                              Present { value: decoded } =>
                                if decoded.rest == "" {
                                  Present {
                                    value: DemandIdentity {
                                      kind: kind_f.value as ArtifactKindId,
                                      subject: subject,
                                      declared_inputs: decoded.inputs
                                    }
                                  }
                                } else {
                                  none
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
      }
  }
}


type JudgmentContract {
  demand_identity: DemandIdentity
  result: ResultContract
  demand_nature: DemandNature
}


fn judgment_required_output_ids(contract: JudgmentContract) -> List<ArtifactOutputId> {
  contract.result.required_persisted_outputs |> map(o => o.id)
}
